# rev: Reverse a line of text or a file.
- Reverse text typed into terminal: rev
- Reverse the text string "hello": echo "hello" | rev
- Reverse an entire file and print to `stdout`: rev {{path/to/file}}
- Use '\0' as a line separator (zero termination): rev {{[-0|--zero]}} {{path/to/file}}
- Display help: rev {{[-h|--help]}}
- Display version: rev {{[-V|--version]}}

# uname: Print details about the current machine and the operating system running on it. See also: `lsb_release`.
- Print kernel name: uname
- Print all available system information: uname {{[-a|--all]}}
- Print system architecture and processor information: uname {{[-mp|--machine --processor]}}
- Print kernel name, kernel release, and kernel version: uname {{[-srv|--kernel-name --kernel-release --kernel-version]}}
- Print system hostname: uname {{[-n|--nodename]}}
- Print the current operating system name: uname {{[-o|--operating-system]}}

