# chsh: Change user's login shell. Part of `util-linux`.
- Set a specific login shell for the current user interactively: chsh
- List available shells: chsh {{[-l|--list-shells]}}
- Set a specific login shell for the current user: chsh {{[-s|--shell]}} {{path/to/shell}}
- Set a login shell for a specific user: sudo chsh {{[-s|--shell]}} {{path/to/shell}} {{username}}

# pwd: Print the name of current/working directory.
- Print the current directory: pwd
- Print the current directory, and resolve all symlinks (i.e. show the "physical" path): pwd {{[-P|--physical]}}
