- Print the second column of the lines matching a pattern in a space-separated file: gawk '/{{pattern}}/ {print $2}' {{path/to/file}}
- Print the last column of each line in a file, using a comma (instead of space) as a field separator: gawk {{[-F|--field-separator]}} ',' '{print $NF}' {{path/to/file}}
