# openssl: OpenSSL cryptographic toolkit. Some subcommands such as `req` have their own usage documentation.
- Generate a private key and encrypt the output file using AES-256: openssl genpkey -algorithm {{rsa|ec}} -out {{path/to/private.key}} -aes256
- Generate the corresponding public key from the private key `private.key` using `rsa`: openssl rsa -in {{path/to/private.key}} -pubout -out {{path/to/public.key}}
- Generate a self-signed certificate valid for a specified number of days (365): openssl req -new -x509 -key {{path/to/private.key}} -out {{path/to/certificate.crt}} -days 365
- Convert a certificate to `.pem` or `.der` format: openssl x509 -in {{path/to/certificate.crt}} -out {{path/to/certificate}}.{{pem|der}} -outform {{pem|der}}
- Check certificate details: openssl x509 -in {{path/to/certificate.crt}} -text -noout
- Generate a certificate signing request (CSR): openssl req -new -key {{path/to/private.key}} -out {{path/to/request.csr}}

