- Extend the file size by 50 MiB, fill with holes (which reads as zero bytes): truncate {{[-s|--size]}} +50M {{path/to/file}}
- Shrink the file by 2 GiB, by removing data from the end of file: truncate {{[-s|--size]}} -2G {{path/to/file}}
- Empty the file's content: truncate {{[-s|--size]}} 0 {{path/to/file}}
