254:
# chown: Change user and group ownership of files and directories. See also: `chgrp`.
- Change the owner user of a file/directory: sudo chown {{user}} {{path/to/file_or_directory}}
- Change the owner user and group of a file/directory: sudo chown {{user}}:{{group}} {{path/to/file_or_directory}}
- Change the owner user and group to both have the name `user`: sudo chown {{user}}: {{path/to/file_or_directory}}
- Change the group of a file to a group that the current user belongs to: chown :{{group}} {{path/to/file_or_directory}}
- Recursively change the owner of a directory and its contents: sudo chown {{[-R|--recursive]}} {{user}} {{path/to/directory}}
